{#
  src/data/index.njk: reference for every machine-readable output. Written from
  compactIndex(), toCsv() and the area split in src/_data/iocIndex.js and the
  templates that emit each file (src/ioc-*.njk, src/repo-scanner-index.njk,
  src/feed.njk, src/sitemap*.njk). If one of those changes a column, a key or
  which records a file holds, this page changes in the same commit. Counts are
  read from iocIndex.
#}
{% set t = iocIndex.totals %}
<section>
  <h1>Data and downloads</h1>
  <p>
    Indicators can be downloaded in bulk in four areas: remote workers
    ({{ t.remote_workers | thousands }}), espionage ({{ t.espionage | thousands }}),
    PolinRider repositories ({{ t.polinrider | thousands }}) and EtherHiding
    ({{ t.etherhiding | thousands }}).
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="files">Files</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="results-table" data-no-sort>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">File</th>
          <th scope="col">Format</th>
          <th scope="col">Records</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="/assets/data/ioc-index.csv">/assets/data/ioc-index.csv</a></th>
          <td>CSV</td>
          <td>Remote workers only ({{ iocIndex.remote_workers.total | thousands }}). See <a href="#csv">CSV columns</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">/assets/data/ioc-index-<em>type</em>.csv</th>
          <td>CSV</td>
          <td>One file per indicator type; see <a href="#csv-by-type">files by type</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="/assets/data/ioc-index.json">/assets/data/ioc-index.json</a></th>
          <td>JSON</td>
          <td>Remote workers, espionage and PolinRider ({{ (t.remote_workers + t.espionage + t.polinrider) | thousands }}). See <a href="#json">JSON keys</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="/assets/data/ioc-search.json">/assets/data/ioc-search.json</a></th>
          <td>JSON</td>
          <td>Records without <code>contexts</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="/assets/data/ioc-contexts.json">/assets/data/ioc-contexts.json</a></th>
          <td>JSON</td>
          <td>The <code>contexts</code> table alone.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="/assets/data/repo-scanner-index.json">/assets/data/repo-scanner-index.json</a></th>
          <td>JSON</td>
          <td>Scan rules and compromised repositories ({{ iocIndex.repo_scanner.total | thousands }}).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="/feed.xml">/feed.xml</a></th>
          <td>Atom</td>
          <td>Profiles and hunts; no indicators.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="/sitemap.xml">/sitemap.xml</a></th>
          <td>XML sitemap index</td>
          <td>Every page address.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="/license.txt">/license.txt</a></th>
          <td>Text</td>
          <td>Licence terms; see <a href="#licence">below</a>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    EtherHiding records have no bulk file; use the
    <a href="/etherhiding/#watchlist">watchlist table</a>. Every record has a
    page under <a href="/indicators/browse/">Browse indicators</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="updates">When the files change</h2>
  <p>
    Files are regenerated on each build. The JSON files carry a
    <code>generated_at</code> timestamp, currently
    {% if iocIndex.generated_at %}<code>{{ iocIndex.generated_at }}</code>{% else %}not set{% endif %}.
    The CSV files carry no date.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="csv">CSV columns</h2>
  <p>
    One row per indicator. Cells that read as formulas are prefixed with an
    apostrophe.
  </p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="results-table" data-no-sort>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Column</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>value</code></th><td>The normalised indicator.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>ioc_type</code></th><td>The type, such as <code>email_address</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>persona</code></th><td>The fabricated identity the value was filed under.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>account_status</code></th><td><code>live</code>, <code>removed</code> or <code>recycled</code> for a checked account. See <a href="/glossary/#label-account-status">account status</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>network</code></th><td>The network kind or VPN provider, for a looked-up IP address. See <a href="/glossary/#label-network-kind">network kinds</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>campaigns</code></th><td>The tagged activity clusters, joined with <code>; </code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>first_seen</code></th><td>The earliest citing-source date.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>last_seen</code></th><td>The latest citing-source date.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>provenance</code></th><td>How the value reached the index, as a code. See <a href="/glossary/#labels-provenance">provenance labels</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>model</code></th><td>The extracting model, for <code>llm</code> provenance.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>source_urls</code></th><td>The citing sources, joined with <code> | </code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>source_titles</code></th><td>Their titles, in the same order.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>context</code></th><td>The passage around the value in each source.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3 id="csv-by-type">Files by type</h3>
  <p>The same columns, one file per type for remote workers:</p>
  <p class="chip-row">
    {% for type, count in iocIndex.remote_workers.counts_by_type %}
    <a class="tag-chip" href="/assets/data/ioc-index-{{ type }}.csv" download>{{ type | replace("_", " ") }} ({{ count | thousands }})</a>
    {% endfor %}
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="json">JSON keys</h2>
  <p>
    ioc-index.json and repo-scanner-index.json share one compact shape. The
    top level holds:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>v</code>, the format version (currently 2), and <code>generated_at</code>;</li>
    <li>the lookup tables <code>types</code>, <code>methods</code>, <code>sources</code> and <code>contexts</code>, referred to by position;</li>
    <li><code>records</code>, with the keys below; absent values are <code>null</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="results-table" data-no-sort>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>i</code></th><td>The record id.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>t</code></th><td>Position in <code>types</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>v</code></th><td>The normalised value.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>d</code></th><td>The value as printed, where it differs.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>r</code></th><td>The area, such as <code>remote-workers</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>p</code></th><td>The persona name.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>h</code></th><td>The persona page slug, for a single persona.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>c</code></th><td>Reserved; empty.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>k</code></th><td>The activity clusters, as a list.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>e</code></th><td>Position in <code>methods</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>g</code></th><td><code>1</code> if found in the source text, otherwise <code>0</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>m</code></th><td><code>live</code> or <code>removed</code>, for a checked repository or package.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>a</code></th><td>For a checked account, its <code>state</code> and <code>checked</code> date.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>n</code></th><td>For an IP address, the network kind and its label.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>w</code></th><td>For an email address, the reported password and reuse-group id.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>f</code>, <code>l</code></th><td>First and last seen.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>rr</code>, <code>rk</code></th><td>For a value no dated source names: the creation date of the account, or of the persona's LinkedIn or GitHub account (<code>rk</code> is <code>linkedin</code> or <code>github</code>), else the day this site first recorded it. The Report date column shows which.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>s</code></th><td>The citations, each a list of source position, context position, retrieval date, section heading and passage origin.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    ioc-search.json omits <code>contexts</code> and any key that is
    <code>null</code>, <code>0</code>, an empty list or an <code>r</code> of
    <code>remote-workers</code>; a missing key means that value.
    ioc-contexts.json holds only <code>v</code>, <code>generated_at</code> and
    <code>contexts</code>.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="stix-misp">STIX 2.1, MISP and other result downloads</h2>
  <p>
    The indicator searches on <a href="/remote-workers/">Remote Workers</a>,
    each cluster page and the <a href="/repo-scanner/">Repo Scanner</a> download
    current results as STIX 2.1, MISP, CSV, text or JSON. These files are built
    in the browser and have no fixed address.
  </p>
</section>

